- The string parameter `secret` and the string parameter `guess` must consist of digits only.
- The length of the string parameter `secret` and the string parameter `guess` is greater than or equal to 1 and is less than or equal to 1000.
- The string parameter `secret` and the string parameter `guess` have the same length.
- The string result is formatted as "xAyB" where x is the number of bulls and y is the number of cows.
- The number of bulls represents the digits in the guess that are in the correct position.
- The number of cows represents the digits in the guess that are in the secret number but are located in the wrong position.
- Only one of the two unmatched digits is counted as a cow if the non-bull digits can only be rearranged to allow one digit to be a bull.